Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:50:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] triage: escalated verdict + scoped escalation pass

- triage.md: a sweep may mark a clear-intent row 'escalated' with its
  findings when the source doesn't yield a confident root cause; an
  escalation pass (ESCALATION_ROW_IDS set) is scoped to those rows, starts
  from the thread, may not escalate again, and bounds its reads.
- claude-triage.yml: escalation/row_ids inputs, scoped snapshot, the
  env var for the agent, and an Escalate step after the reap that flips
  escalated rows to triaging and calls the Worker's escalate_triage
  (failing them visibly if the Worker is missing or refuses).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
